# GHManager configuration
#
# Optional: a GitHub Personal Access Token used as the default identity for the
# dashboard. If this is set, GHManager starts already authenticated and the
# token never leaves the server. If it is omitted, paste a token into the UI
# instead - it is stored in an httpOnly cookie that browser JavaScript cannot
# read.
#
# Required token scopes:
#   Classic PAT ...... repo  (full control of private repositories)
#   Fine-grained PAT . Repository permissions -> Contents: Read and write,
#                      Pull requests: Read and write, Metadata: Read-only
#
# Create one at https://github.com/settings/tokens
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Optional: point at a GitHub Enterprise Server installation.
# Defaults to the public github.com endpoints.
# GITHUB_API_BASE_URL=https://github.example.com/api/v3
# GITHUB_GRAPHQL_URL=https://github.example.com/api/graphql
